WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.820
So the one other moment I want to show you
from this Trump propaganda press briefing

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:09.790
that he did over the weekend, that it is a
Bedminster golf club goes very simply to Donald

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:14.840
Trump's completely thin skin and his complete
inability to face any serious challenges to

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:15.840
his lies.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.360
Now, if you watch the Jonathan Swane Axios
interview recently, you already know that

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:25.470
Donald Trump completely implodes when subjected
to even the most minor fact checking.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:30.490
But in the interview with Jonathan Swann,
he wasn't really able to do what he did when

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.809
CBS is Paula Reid confronted him.

00:00:32.809 --> 00:00:34.649
Now, as I told you in the last segment.

00:00:34.649 --> 00:00:39.829
Donald Trump has been regularly taking credit
for Barack Obama's policy veterans choice.

00:00:39.829 --> 00:00:42.200
Obama signed it into law in 2014.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.239
Trump regularly takes credit for it as if
it's something that he did.

00:00:45.239 --> 00:00:50.660
Well, CBS News, as Paula Reid was not having
it and she called him out, and you will see

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:55.800
how Donald Trump reacted about being confronted
about such such an obvious and overt lie.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.070
He does not take it well.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:58.340
Take a look.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:00:59.930
I mean, veterans.

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:07.119
John's choice, it was passed in 2010 excuse
me.

00:01:07.119 --> 00:01:08.720
Go ahead.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.710
It's a false statement, sir.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:16.710
Thank you very much, everybody.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:19.109
Thank you for.

00:01:19.109 --> 00:01:22.840
So Trump just walks off abruptly.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.020
This is how fragile authoritarian dictators
behave.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.509
They pretend to be alpha and powerful.

00:01:30.509 --> 00:01:36.900
And then when their wild claims are subjected
to scrutiny, they abort the situation.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.259
Essentially now in some places, they'll also
have the journalists killed.

00:01:40.259 --> 00:01:42.509
I don't expect that to happen to Paul Reid.

00:01:42.509 --> 00:01:47.149
But Trump shrinks like a frightened turtle
and recedes into his shell.

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:53.679
This persona of big power and strength very
quickly falls apart when you confront him

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:56.090
and make him face his obvious lies.

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:57.929
And in this case, Donald Trump just walks
off.

00:01:57.929 --> 00:02:04.200
Now, it also shouldn't be ignored that the
entire setup for this with the crowd of club

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:10.929
goers cheering Trump and booing the media,
it's scaling up yet another level, the degree

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:15.500
of sycophancy that's constructed around Donald
Trump all the time.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.180
But I actually think that this is something
reporters should use to their advantage.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:24.739
We've now seen Trump end press conferences
multiple times when a reporter is allowed

00:02:24.739 --> 00:02:27.540
by other reporters to follow up.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:33.239
And what Trump counts on is that when he's
done with reporter number one, even if they

00:02:33.239 --> 00:02:34.450
try to follow up.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:38.700
I was going to say, even if she tries to follow
up, usually this tends to happen with women.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:43.840
He'll go to the next reporter and the next
reporter is often so desperate to ask their

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.730
question that they just immediately launch
in.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:51.280
But when it doesn't happen, when a reporter
says, no, no, you can follow up.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:53.709
It's often led to the end of a press briefing.

00:02:53.709 --> 00:03:01.480
I remember this happened to CBS as Wadia Giang,
who was, I believe, Caitlin Collins from CNN,

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:06.410
allowed Wade Geia to follow up about something
related to China that Trump said to her, and

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:09.409
she's Chinese American and it didn't go well.

00:03:09.409 --> 00:03:14.560
This happened to Caitlyn Collins when she
was allowed to follow up by another reporter.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:15.810
And Trump tried to move on.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:17.269
Ended up bailing on the press briefing.

00:03:17.269 --> 00:03:20.030
And it's happened several times and again
this weekend.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:24.870
And reporters should really make an implicit
agreement with themselves.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:30.629
Let's allow each other to follow up even when
Donald Trump tries to call on the next person

00:03:30.629 --> 00:03:35.560
and then he's going to end up bailing altogether
even more than he does when he is confronted

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:38.180
by facts, he frequently runs away.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:45.079
And yet many of his 63 million supporters
from 2016 still see a strong alpha male there.

00:03:45.079 --> 00:03:48.980
And seeing this actually makes me curious
about Trump's interest in debating.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:50.939
He had to debate in 2016.

00:03:50.939 --> 00:03:56.400
There was no way in 2016 as the challenger,
as the nonincumbent to say, I'm not going

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.400
to debate Hillary Clinton.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.110
I don't think he could have gotten away with
it.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:03.109
But right now, Donald Trump clearly does not
want counterpoints.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:06.860
He doesn't want a scenario in which he could
be called out about his lies or fact check

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:08.180
to any degree.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:14.499
My expectation is that if Donald Trump does
debate, his team will work very hard to keep

00:04:14.499 --> 00:04:19.650
the rebuttals short and to put in place all
sorts of rules that will favor Trump, including

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:23.620
no fact checking by the moderators.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:29.669
And if not, I would not be surprised to see
him find a reason out of the debates.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:05:35.729
The most likely scenario is he will get what
he wants and the debates

00:05:35.729 --> 00:06:20.430
will happen.

